  "composer": {
    "accepted_prose": "Tomi let the silence hold. She didn't look away. The shift was unexpected—he'd pulled back the weight of choosing, of managing something she hadn't asked to manage. It wasn't forgiveness, not yet, and she wouldn't call it relief. But the pressure had eased, leaving space she hadn't realized was missing. She ran her thumb along her sleeve, feeling the fabric, letting the moment settle. Her curiosity remained, cool and private, beneath the surface.\n\nFinally, she spoke. 'Okay.' A single word, even. Then, with a half-shrug that didn't quite hide the edge of a smile: 'I get it. You don't have to wait around for me to figure stuff out.' She paused, letting that land. 'If I want something, I'll say so. When I'm ready.' Her tone was casual, but the words were deliberate—a line drawn, not a door closed. She didn't offer more. The exchange settled into a quiet that felt like agreement.",
